Given the Wage interface, Employee class and main method below, what will be printed?

```java
public interface Wage {
  default void notice() { System.out.println("Executing..."); }
  void increase();
}
public class Employee implements Wage {
  private String id;
  private String name;
  private int salary;
  public Employee(String id, String name) {
    this.id = id;
    this.name = name;
    this.salary = 1000;
  }
  @Override
  public void notice() {
    System.out.println("Employee salary computed!");
  }
  @Override
  public void increase() {
    this.salary += 200;
  }
  /* GETTERS AND SETTERS */
}
public static void main(String[] args) {
  Employee e = new Employee("EMP101", "John Doe");
  try {
    e.increase();
    System.out.println("Salary: " + e.getSalary());
  } catch (Exception ex) {
    System.out.println("Cannot increase/decrease salary.");
  } finally {
    e.notice();
  }
}
```

